      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In the late 1980s, two long-distance runners in California mixed "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "vitamins",
            "zh": "维生素"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "oat bran",
            "zh": "燕麦糠"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "milk protein",
            "zh": "蛋白质"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "corn syrup",
            "zh": "糖浆"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in their kitchen. They ended up with a PowerBar, one of the world’s first protein bars. The invention soon became popular with gym-goers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, protein bars are everywhere, and they are not just for gym-goers. Instead, they are sold as healthy snacks. Their "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "manufacturers",
            "ref": "v-manufacturer"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " want you to believe that they can improve not just your workout but also your health. But are protein bars really that good?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There’s no question that our bodies need protein for building and repairing "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "muscles",
            "zh": "肌肉"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Protein also makes up our hair, nails, skin, and other "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "organs",
            "zh": "器官"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The amino acids in protein help our brains work properly. Perhaps because of that, many people set protein side by side with fitness. When they eat protein bars, they really believe that they are doing something good for their health."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But according to Dr Eric Rimm, a health expert, hardly anyone needs extra protein if they eat meat. Most meat eaters get far more than the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "recommended",
            "ref": "v-recommend"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " daily amount of protein. Even those who don’t eat meat can get enough protein from tofu and nuts."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Protein bars are often full of sugar. A 70-gram chocolate protein bar, for example, may contain 15 to 30 grams of added sugar. “Many protein bars are really just candy bars with a lot more protein,” says Dr Rimm. “They are highly processed.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Not all protein bars are created equal, though. If you really want one as a snack, pay attention to the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nutrition facts label",
            "zh": "营养成分表"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Choose those with lots of nuts and fruit and less than five grams of added sugar. And always remember that grapes, bananas, apples, and nuts can be much better snacks than protein bars."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
